-- title:
--   Fibre of the R-class set over a Λ₁-class
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and write $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ and $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}=\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^f$, where $\mathbb{A}^f$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ satisfying `IsOrder`, i.e. containing $1$, closed under multiplication, finitely generated, and with $\mathbb{Q}$-span all of $\mathbb{H}$; let $m,x\in\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$, and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule with $R=\Lambda_1\cap\{z\in\mathbb{H}: z\otimes 1\in m\,\widehat{\Lambda_1}\,m^{-1}\}$, where $\widehat{\Lambda}$ denotes the additive subgroup `finiteAdeleBox` of $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}$ generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ integral at every finite place. For a submodule $\Lambda$ put $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}:=$ `finiteIdeleStabilizer` $\Lambda$, the stabiliser of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ in $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$, and $\mathrm{Cl}(\Lambda):=$ `ClassSet`, the double coset set of $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}$ by the diagonal image of $\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ on the left and $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$ on the right; `classSetForget` is the map $\mathrm{Cl}(R)\to\mathrm{Cl}(\Lambda_1)$ sending a class to the $\widehat{\Lambda_1}^{\times}$-class of a chosen representative. The assertion is that there is a bijection $e$ from the fibre $\{c\in\mathrm{Cl}(R): \text{image of } c \text{ in } \mathrm{Cl}(\Lambda_1)=[x]\}$ onto the quotient of $\{J\subset\mathbb{H}: J=\mathbb{H}\cap xum\widehat{\Lambda_1}\text{ for some }u\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}^{\times}\}$ by the relation $J\sim J'$ iff $J'=\delta\cdot J$ for some $\delta\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ with $x^{-1}\delta x\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}^{\times}$ (the units of the left order of $\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda_1}$), and moreover $e$ is given explicitly: for every $u\in\widehat{\Lambda_1}^{\times}$ whose $R$-class $[xu]$ lies in the fibre, $e([xu])$ is the class of $\mathbb{H}\cap xum\widehat{\Lambda_1}$. Here $\mathbb{H}\cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$ abbreviates `ofFiniteIdele`, the submodule $\{z\in\mathbb{H}: z\otimes 1\in g\widehat{\Lambda}\}$.
--
--   This is the quaternionic half of the level-$N$ Deuring–Eichler dictionary: a class of the order $R=\Lambda_1\cap m\Lambda_1m^{-1}$ lying over a given class of $\Lambda_1$ is the same datum as a type-$m$ sublattice of the right $\Lambda_1$-ideal attached to $x$, taken up to the units of its left order. It is used in the identification of the class set of $R$ with the set of supersingular places of the relevant moduli object.
